  - _legacySwatchName: Default
    _legacyColorId: Error
    _canonicalTokenId: status/error/text
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 5 uses, 4 of them TextMeshPro.
  - _legacySwatchName: Default
    _legacyColorId: Warning
    _canonicalTokenId: status/warning/fill
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: "One use, a 3D Renderer \u2014 the only material-path binding in the project."
  - _legacySwatchName: Default
    _legacyColorId: Success
    _canonicalTokenId: status/success/fill
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: Unused in content; aliased so any future reference resolves.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: 100
    _canonicalTokenId: text/primary
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: Byte-identical to Default.Text at 8 bits in both variants, so the two
      collapse.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: 80
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/wash-strong
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 4 uses, 3 of them Image.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: 60
    _canonicalTokenId: text/muted
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 23 uses, 17 of them TextMeshPro. Dark is byte-identical; Light is deliberately
      0.67 rather than V1's 0.60, which failed WCAG AA at 3.80:1.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: 40
    _canonicalTokenId: text/subtle
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 9 uses, 6 of them TextMeshPro. Dark is byte-identical; Light is deliberately
      0.53 rather than V1's 0.40, which failed even the large-text threshold at 2.28:1.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: 20
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/wash-subtle
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 8 uses and every one is an Image. Despite the swatch name this is a fill,
      not text.
  - _legacySwatchName: Text
    _legacyColorId: Secondary
    _canonicalTokenId: text/muted
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: "A pair the V1 vocabulary never defined \u2014 Text carried only {20,40,60,80,100}
      \u2014 so it has always resolved to the magenta sentinel. One use: Confirmation
      Detailed's Cancel button, overriding an instance of Button.prefab whose own
      ColorID is Text.60. Since Text.60 already aliases to text/muted, whose authored
      description is literally \"Secondary text\", the override was the author naming
      the source's own colour and mistyping the key. Aliased here rather than deleted
      so the intent survives; it renders as the source always intended. Decided 2026-08-02."
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 20
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/sunken
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 8 uses, all Image.
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 60
    _canonicalTokenId: border/default
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 5 uses, all Image.
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 100
    _canonicalTokenId: action/pressed/fill
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: One use, a ColorIDButton pressed state.
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 0
    _canonicalTokenId: palette/neutral/0
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: Unused; maps to a primitive.
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 40
    _canonicalTokenId: palette/neutral/400
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: Unused; maps to a primitive.
  - _legacySwatchName: Gray
    _legacyColorId: 80
    _canonicalTokenId: palette/neutral/800
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: Unused; maps to a primitive.
  - _legacySwatchName: Black
    _legacyColorId: 40
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/scrim
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 4 uses split 2 Image / 2 TextMeshPro. Black at 40% is an overlay idiom,
      so it maps to a scrim; the 2 text uses are the least certain mapping in this
      table and want review.
  - _legacySwatchName: Black
    _legacyColorId: 60
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/scrim-medium
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 'Missed by the first vocabulary pass: the Phase 0 inventory''s text scan
      does not see a legacy pair carried as a prefab-instance override, and EnterPIN''s
      Cancel Button carries one. It was therefore resolving to the magenta sentinel
      under V2. Black at 0.6 alpha, so the alias restores exactly what V1 rendered.'
  - _legacySwatchName: Black
    _legacyColorId: 80
    _canonicalTokenId: surface/scrim-strong
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: 2 uses, both Image.
  - _legacySwatchName: Black
    _legacyColorId: 100
    _canonicalTokenId: palette/neutral/1000
    _deprecatedSince: 1.18.0
    _removalVersion: 2.0.0
    _note: "Missed for the same reason as Black.60 \u2014 carried only as a prefab-instance
      override, which the inventory's text scan does not see \u2014 so it too was
      resolving to magenta. One use: ContentPackage List Item's pressed state. The
      scrim ramp stops at 80 because a scrim is by definition translucent, so fully
      opaque black maps to the neutral primitive instead. Decided 2026-08-02."
  _accessibilityRequirements:
  - _foregroundTokenId: text/primary
    _backgroundTokenId: surface/canvas
    _minimumRatio: 4.5
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: palette/shell/base
    _rationale: Body text on the window background. Measures about 14:1 in Dark.
    _severity: 2
  - _foregroundTokenId: text/primary
    _backgroundTokenId: surface/panel
    _minimumRatio: 4.5
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: 
    _rationale: Body text on an opaque panel.
    _severity: 2
  - _foregroundTokenId: text/muted
    _backgroundTokenId: surface/canvas
    _minimumRatio: 4.5
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: palette/shell/base
    _rationale: Secondary text on the window background. Measures 5.86:1 in Dark.
      Light failed at 3.80:1 under V1's single-alpha value; raising the Light alpha
      to 0.67 reaches 4.62:1, so this is now locked at Error in both variants.
    _severity: 2
  - _foregroundTokenId: text/subtle
    _backgroundTokenId: surface/canvas
    _minimumRatio: 3
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: palette/shell/base
    _rationale: De-emphasised text, held to the large-text threshold by design. Measures
      3.38:1 in Dark. Light failed at 2.28:1 under V1's single-alpha value; raising
      the Light alpha to 0.53 reaches 3.16:1. Locked at Error so neither variant
      can regress.
    _severity: 2
  - _foregroundTokenId: action/primary/on-fill
    _backgroundTokenId: action/primary/fill
    _minimumRatio: 4.5
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: 
    _rationale: Label on a primary button. The per-variant alias is what makes this
      pass in both.
    _severity: 2
  - _foregroundTokenId: status/error/text
    _backgroundTokenId: surface/canvas
    _minimumRatio: 3
    _appliesToVariants: []
    _underSurfaceTokenId: palette/shell/base
    _rationale: "Error text on the window background measures about 4.0:1 in Dark
      \u2014 short of 4.5:1. Recorded as a warning rather than an error because this
      is the shipped V1 value; darkening the red or lightening the canvas is a design
      decision."
    _severity: 1
